menu "KVS WebRTC Configuration"

    config ENABLE_DATA_CHANNEL
        bool "Enable Data channel support using usrsctp"
        default y
        help
            Enables WebRTC Data channel support

    config USE_ESP_TLS_FOR_KVS
        bool "Use ESP-TLS for KVS TLS connections (TURN over TLS)"
        default y
        help
            Use ESP-TLS implementation instead of direct mbedTLS for TLS connections.
            This enables the use of ESP certificate bundle for CA verification,
            eliminating the need for certificate files on the filesystem.
            Recommended for ESP platforms to avoid certificate management complexity.

    config KVS_TRANSPORT_INSTRUMENTATION
        bool "Log transport timing and state every few seconds"
        default n
        help
            Periodic reports from the DTLS, ICE and SCTP layers: per-packet
            encrypt and send timing, connectivity checks offered against
            answered, the negotiated reliability of each data channel, what
            partial reliability abandoned, and the association's congestion
            window, receive window, smoothed RTT and path MTU.

            Off by default because it prints every five seconds on several
            layers at once and will bury anything else in the log.

            Worth turning on whenever a connection is up but not moving data.
            The congestion window sitting at exactly one MTU is the signature
            of every full-size packet being lost, which reads nothing like
            congestion from the outside and is otherwise slow to find.
endmenu
